menuconfig SYSTEMCMDS_SECURE_MAVLINK_ENROLL
	bool "secure_mavlink_enroll"
	default n
	depends on LIB_SECURE_MAVLINK
	---help---
		Enrol this aircraft for secure MAVLink: read the link
		public key out, and write the ground station key and the identity
		payload back in. The ground end is ztcs-mavlink-provision.

menuconfig USER_SECURE_MAVLINK_ENROLL
	bool "secure_mavlink_enroll running as userspace module"
	default y
	depends on BOARD_PROTECTED && SYSTEMCMDS_SECURE_MAVLINK_ENROLL
	---help---
		Put secure_mavlink_enroll in userspace memory. It reaches the
		keystore through the crypto ioctls, like MAVLink, and in the
		kernel it would carry a second copy of the Noise core beside the
		kernel layer's own.
